  resstring UIString helpString {
    id = 1027, text = "TIMEBOARD TIME SERVICE\n\nTimeBoard Time Service (TBTS) provides Internet time synchronization for TimeBoard and compatible Palm OS devices.\n\nTBTS retrieves the current Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) from the Internet, applies the selected GMT offset, and sets the Palm system clock.\n\n · TIME SYNC\nTap \"Time Sync\" to connect to TBTS and synchronize the Palm clock.\n\nThe app retrieves the current UTC time, applies your GMT offset and updates the system date and time.\n\n · API & SERVICE VERSION\nAfter a successful synchronization, the app displays the API and Service versions reported by TBTS.\n\nThese values are saved and represent the last successful response received from the server. They are updated after a successful synchronization if the server version changes.\n\n · GMT OFFSET\nSelect the GMT offset corresponding to your current location before using Time Sync.\n\nTBTS provides UTC time. This offset converts it to your local time before setting the Palm clock.\n\nIf you change time zones, select the new offset before synchronizing.\n\n · RETRY ATTEMPTS\nSets how many times the app will retry after a connection failure. Valid values are 1 to 9.\n\nHigher values may help with slow or unstable connections. Some server errors are not automatically retried.\n\n · CONNECTION STATUS\nThe connection indicator shows whether the app is connecting, synchronization succeeded, or an error occurred.\n\n · ERRORS\nErrors may occur if Internet access is unavailable, the server cannot be reached, DNS resolution fails, the connection is interrupted, or an invalid response is received.\n\nNetwork errors may include a Palm OS error code to help identify the problem.\n\nHTTP error 429 (Too Many Requests) means too many requests were sent in a short time. Wait before trying again.\n\n · TIMEBOARD\nTBTS works together with TimeBoard. TimeBoard provides clock, calendar and other time-related features, while TBTS provides Internet time synchronization for compatible Palm OS devices.\n\n · INTERNET CONNECTION\nTime Sync requires an active Internet connection through any networking method supported by the Palm device.\n\nPreviously saved settings and API/Service version information remain available without an Internet connection.\n\n · PRIVACY\nNo account, login or authentication is required for time synchronization.\n\nFor more information, visit:\ntbts.coloraturip.com"
  }
